"""s58 -- does a two-layer producer (ordered prefix/suffix wrapper over a local-memory core stream) predict untouched pages?

PRE-REGISTERED QUESTION (frozen in s58_two_layer_heldout.prereg.sha256 BEFORE any fitting on real pages; before the
freeze this script ran only on its synthetic fixture, `--fixture`, which reads no real data):
"A two-layer producer TL -- a core stream generated by s57's local-memory copy-and-vary mechanism (W = 20) and a
separate affix wrapper that chooses EVERY token's prefix and suffix from counted transition tables conditioned on the
previous token's affixes and on line position -- fitted ONLY on the 166 training pages, is asked to predict s57's six
properties of the 41 held-out pages it never sees.  Does it predict >= 5 of 6, with the same calls on all three
transliterations?"

CONTEXT: s57 (results_s57.txt) -- local-memory copy-and-vary alone holds 0/6 on ZL3b, RF1b, IT2a; its p_copy = 0 null
holds 1/6.  s36 (results_s36_two_layer_operator_core.txt, Part 2B) -- a two-layer operator-over-core producer reaches
F1, Moran and (on some seeds) CHARWIN in-sample.  s58 is the first test of a two-layer architecture on untouched pages.

SPLIT: g1_edge_joint.split_names (random.Random(20261017)), 166 / 41 (IT2a 165 / 41).  Everything below is estimated
on the training pages only; held-out pages are touched only by the scoring code (s57's Measured, imported verbatim).

PRODUCER TL (fixed before hashing)
  Segmenter: scoreboard/metrics_new.SlotSegmenter fitted on the training tokens; every training token -> (pre, core, suf).
  CORE LAYER (s57's mechanism, applied to the core stream instead of whole words):
    line-initial core: drawn from the training line-initial core distribution (never copied);
    each next core: with probability p_copy a copy of an earlier core on the same page:
        with probability a (if the line above is long enough) the same-position core on the line above,
        else the core d back in the page core stream (crossing line ends), d in 1..min(W, history),
        P(d) ~ exp(-(d-1)/tau);
      the copied core is passed through s57's core 1-glyph edit with probability q_core (substitution / insertion /
      deletion 1/3 each, deletion only if >= 2 glyphs, else substitution; glyph from the training core-glyph
      distribution), else kept verbatim;
    otherwise (1 - p_copy) a fresh core drawn from the training core lexicon by token frequency.
    W = 20 fixed.  Free parameters: p_copy, tau, a, q_core = 4 (<= 7).
  WRAPPER LAYER (counted, not tuned; 0 free parameters): for every token, the pair (pre, suf) is drawn from
      P(pre, suf | pos, pre_{t-1}, suf_{t-1}), pos in {I (line-initial), M (medial), F (line-final)},
    estimated by counting training lines (lines of length 1 -> I; length 2 -> I, F).  Line-initial tokens are
    conditioned on pos only (no previous token within the line).  Sparse contexts back off by Witten-Bell
    interpolation (parameter free: stay at a context with probability N / (N + T), N = tokens, T = distinct outcomes
    seen in that context, else back off):  (pos, pre_{t-1}, suf_{t-1}) -> (pos, suf_{t-1}) -> (pos) -> (all positions).
  Token = pre + core + suf.  Line lengths: empirical training line-length distribution (as s57).  Page line counts as s57.
  Ported from s36 (TwoLayerModel): the w = P + C + S two-layer word; position-conditioned line-initial / line-final
    operator pools induced from the training pages; a lag-1 cross-word dependence carried by the operator layer.
  DIFFERENCES FROM s36's wrapper (stated before the run): s36 draws 8 whole-word candidates (section lexicon / page
    pool, nb mutation) and reweights them by an R_la_syll cross-boundary glyph table ^1.5, an affix-length cadence
    AR(1) target (|P|+|S|+0.35|C|, gamma 0.56, 0.35/0.65 update), and core anti-repetition (x0.035 if the core is
    already on the line); its edge operators are hand-weighted glyph rewrites (para gallows 46 %, line-initial
    y/d/o/s/q 36 %, line-final -m 14.5 %); it uses (hand, section) operator weights, M2 synthetic rare forms (lam
    calibrated to a type target) and a habit table.  s58 replaces all of these with ONE counted table P(pre, suf |
    pos, previous affixes) (no hand constants, no section / hand conditioning, no glyph-edge table, no length
    cadence term, no anti-repetition), and the core comes from s57's local-memory stream, not a top-220 core pool.

FITTING (training pages only): exactly s57's targets and loss (s57.fit_stats / s57.loss imported): T1 core repetition
  ratio R(d), d = 1..20; T2 edit-type shares among near-repeat pairs (identical / prefix-only / suffix-only / core
  1-edit); T3 type count; T4 line lengths by construction.  Loss = mean_d ((R_g-R_r)/.01)^2 + mean_k
  ((share_g-share_r)/.01)^2 + ((V_g-V_r)/V_r/.01)^2.  Staged grid as s57, seed 0, common random numbers:
    A: q_core = 0.25, grid p_copy x tau x a (s57's grids); B: at A's best, q_core in {0, 0.1, ..., 1.0} (s57's simplex
    reduced to its core axis: q_pre / q_suf do not exist in TL, the wrapper chooses all affixes);
    C: at the best q_core, p_copy x tau x a within +-2 / +-1 / +-1 grid steps of A's best.  Per transliteration.
  Fitted parameters -> runs/s58/fit_<T>.json.

PREDICTIONS: exactly s57's P1-P6, pass rules, intervals (80 % page subsampling without replacement, 500 draws,
  np.random.default_rng(20261017 + offset), same offsets as s57), s15 width [0.1447, 0.2156] for P4 and the s39 rule
  for P6, computed by s57's own scoring code (s57.Measured, s57.draws_for, s57.score_cells imported).  Generated texts
  seeds 1-3: 166 training-like pages + 41 held-out-like pages, each scored like the real text (segmenter and models
  refitted on the generated training pages).
COMPARATORS: (a) TL0 = same wrapper, cores with p_copy = 0 (fresh core draws only), seeds 1-3, scored identically;
  (b) s57 as filed (results_s57.txt; not rerun): local-memory 0/6 on all three, null 1/6.
VERDICT RULE: "two-layer model predicts untouched pages" iff >= 5 of 6 hold on ZL3b AND on RF1b and IT2a the SAME set
  of predictions holds as on ZL3b; if ZL3b >= 5 but RF1b / IT2a differ: "holds on ZL3b only, not stable across
  transliterations"; else "two-layer model does NOT predict untouched pages".  Also reported: per prediction and
  transliteration, which ones TL holds that TL0 does not (and the reverse).
CAVEATS stated before the run: P6 is weak (s57: on the real text of this split the s39 rule itself gives 'affix
  layer' on ZL3b, 'core layer' on RF1b, 'both / neither' on IT2a); P4 is close to built-in (the wrapper's line-initial
  prefix table and the line-initial core table are counted from the training pages); P3 (prefix-stream bigram gain)
  is close to built-in for TL and TL0 alike because the wrapper is a prefix/suffix bigram table -- TL vs TL0 isolates
  the core-memory contribution.
IN-SAMPLE SANITY: TL's fitted R(d), d = 1..20, edit shares and type count against the training targets (printed).

Run:    python -I s58_two_layer_heldout.py [--fixture]
Writes: results_s58.txt, runs/s58/ (fit_<T>.json, sidecars TL_<T>_s<seed>.meta.json and TL0_<T>_s<seed>.meta.json,
        cells.json; fixture.txt and fixture/ for --fixture).  Nothing else.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import json
import math
import random
import sys
import time
from collections import Counter, OrderedDict, defaultdict
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))
for _s in (sys.stdout, sys.stderr):
    try:
        _s.reconfigure(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
        pass

import g1_edge_joint as G1  # noqa: E402
import s57_local_memory_model as S57  # noqa: E402  (scoring, fit statistics, loss, edit operator: verbatim)
from scoreboard.metrics_new import SlotSegmenter  # noqa: E402

SELF = ROOT / "s58_two_layer_heldout.py"
STUB = ROOT / "s58_two_layer_heldout.prereg.sha256"
OUT = ROOT / "results_s58.txt"
RUNS = ROOT / "runs" / "s58"
W = S57.W
STEP_LIMIT = 30 * 60
TRANSLITS = S57.TRANSLITS
GRID_P, GRID_TAU, GRID_A = S57.GRID_P, S57.GRID_TAU, S57.GRID_A
GRID_QC = [i / 10 for i in range(11)]
EDIT_KINDS = S57.EDIT_KINDS
LABELS = ("TL", "TL0")
log: list[str] = []


def emit(s=""):
    print(s, flush=True)
    log.append(s)


def sha256(p: Path) -> str:
    return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def stub_match() -> str:
    if not STUB.exists():
        return "NO STUB"
    want = {}
    for ln in STUB.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
        ln = ln.strip()
        if not ln or ln.startswith("#"):
            continue
        h, f = ln.split(None, 1)
        want[f.lstrip("*").strip()] = h
    bad = [f for f, h in want.items() if not (ROOT / f).exists() or sha256(ROOT / f) != h]
    return "True" if want and not bad else f"False (mismatch: {', '.join(bad) or 'empty stub'})"


def _cum(counter):
    items = sorted(counter.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], str(kv[0])))
    ws = [k for k, _ in items]
    cum, t = [], 0
    for _, c in items:
        t += c; cum.append(t)
    return ws, cum


def pos_of(i, L):
    return "I" if i == 0 else ("F" if i == L - 1 else "M")


# ======================================================================= wrapper (counted)
class Wrapper:
    """P(pre, suf | pos, pre_prev, suf_prev), Witten-Bell back-off -> (pos, suf_prev) -> (pos) -> all."""

    def __init__(self, train_pages, seg):
        c2, c1, c0, call = defaultdict(Counter), defaultdict(Counter), defaultdict(Counter), Counter()
        for lines in train_pages:
            for l in lines:
                sg = [seg.segment(w) for w in l]
                L = len(l)
                for i, (p, _, s) in enumerate(sg):
                    pos = pos_of(i, L)
                    o = (p, s)
                    call[o] += 1
                    c0[pos][o] += 1
                    if i > 0:
                        pp, _, ps = sg[i - 1]
                        c1[(pos, ps)][o] += 1
                        c2[(pos, pp, ps)][o] += 1
        self.levels = []
        for tab in (c2, c1, c0):
            self.levels.append({k: (*_cum(v), sum(v.values()) / (sum(v.values()) + len(v))) for k, v in tab.items()})
        self.all = _cum(call)
        self.sizes = dict(ctx2=len(c2), ctx1=len(c1), ctx0=len(c0), outcomes=len(call))

    def draw(self, rng, pos, prev):
        keys = [None, None, pos] if prev is None else [(pos, prev[0], prev[1]), (pos, prev[1]), pos]
        for lev, k in zip(self.levels, keys):
            if k is None:
                continue
            e = lev.get(k)
            if e is None:
                continue
            ws, cum, lam = e
            if rng.random() < lam:
                return rng.choices(ws, cum_weights=cum)[0]
        return rng.choices(self.all[0], cum_weights=self.all[1])[0]


# ======================================================================= two-layer producer
class TLProducer:
    def __init__(self, train_pages, seg):
        self.seg = seg
        start, lexc, gl = Counter(), Counter(), Counter()
        for lines in train_pages:
            for l in lines:
                for i, w in enumerate(l):
                    c = seg.segment(w)[1]
                    lexc[c] += 1
                    if i == 0:
                        start[c] += 1
                    for ch in c:
                        gl[ch] += 1
        self.start_w, self.start_c = _cum(start)
        self.lex_w, self.lex_c = _cum(lexc)
        self.gl_w, self.gl_c = _cum(gl)
        self.lens = [len(l) for lines in train_pages for l in lines]
        self.wrap = Wrapper(train_pages, seg)
        self.set_params(dict(p_copy=0.0, tau=1.0, a=0.0, q_core=0.25))

    def set_params(self, prm):
        self.prm = dict(prm)
        self.kcum, t = [], 0.0
        for d in range(1, W + 1):
            t += math.exp(-(d - 1) / prm["tau"]); self.kcum.append(t)

    def _swap(self, rng, cur, ws, cum):
        for _ in range(30):
            x = rng.choices(ws, cum_weights=cum)[0]
            if x != cur:
                return x
        return cur

    def core_edit(self, rng, core):
        """s57 Producer.edit, core branch (verbatim logic)."""
        op = rng.randrange(3)
        if op == 2 and len(core) < 2:
            op = 0
        i = rng.randrange(len(core) + (1 if op == 1 else 0))
        if op == 0:
            g = self._swap(rng, core[i], self.gl_w, self.gl_c)
            return core[:i] + g + core[i + 1:]
        if op == 1:
            g = rng.choices(self.gl_w, cum_weights=self.gl_c)[0]
            return core[:i] + g + core[i:]
        return core[:i] + core[i + 1:]

    def page(self, rng, n_lines):
        p = self.prm
        hist, clines, lines = [], [], []
        for _ in range(n_lines):
            L = rng.choice(self.lens)
            cl, line, prev = [], [], None
            for i in range(L):
                if i == 0:
                    c = rng.choices(self.start_w, cum_weights=self.start_c)[0]
                elif p["p_copy"] > 0 and rng.random() < p["p_copy"]:
                    if clines and len(clines[-1]) > i and rng.random() < p["a"]:
                        src = clines[-1][i]
                    else:
                        h = min(W, len(hist))
                        d = rng.choices(range(1, h + 1), cum_weights=self.kcum[:h])[0]
                        src = hist[-d]
                    c = self.core_edit(rng, src) if rng.random() < p["q_core"] else src
                else:
                    c = rng.choices(self.lex_w, cum_weights=self.lex_c)[0]
                pre, suf = self.wrap.draw(rng, pos_of(i, L), prev)
                prev = (pre, suf)
                cl.append(c); hist.append(c); line.append(pre + c + suf)
            clines.append(cl); lines.append(line)
        return lines

    def text(self, seed, page_line_counts):
        rng = random.Random(seed)
        return [self.page(rng, n) for n in page_line_counts]


def fit(train_pages, seg, emit_fn, budget_t0):
    enc = S57.Encoder(seg)
    real = S57.fit_stats(train_pages, enc)
    prod = TLProducer(train_pages, seg)
    counts = [len(l) for l in train_pages]
    cache = {}

    def evaluate(prm):
        key = tuple(round(prm[k], 6) for k in ("p_copy", "tau", "a", "q_core"))
        if key in cache:
            return cache[key]
        prod.set_params(prm)
        g = S57.fit_stats(prod.text(0, counts), enc)
        L, parts = S57.loss(g, real)
        cache[key] = (L, parts, g)
        if time.time() - budget_t0 > STEP_LIMIT:
            raise TimeoutError("fitting step exceeded 30 minutes")
        return cache[key]

    best = None
    for pc in GRID_P:
        for tau in GRID_TAU:
            for a in GRID_A:
                prm = dict(p_copy=pc, tau=tau, a=a, q_core=0.25)
                L = evaluate(prm)[0]
                if best is None or L < best[0]:
                    best = (L, prm)
    emit_fn(f"    stage A ({len(cache)} evals): best loss {best[0]:.2f} at p_copy {best[1]['p_copy']}, tau {best[1]['tau']}, a {best[1]['a']}")
    bA = best[1]
    for qc in GRID_QC:
        prm = dict(bA, q_core=qc)
        L = evaluate(prm)[0]
        if L < best[0]:
            best = (L, prm)
    emit_fn(f"    stage B ({len(cache)} evals): best loss {best[0]:.2f} at q_core {best[1]['q_core']}")
    qc = best[1]["q_core"]
    ip, it, ia = GRID_P.index(bA["p_copy"]), GRID_TAU.index(bA["tau"]), GRID_A.index(bA["a"])
    for pc in GRID_P[max(0, ip - 2): ip + 3]:
        for tau in GRID_TAU[max(0, it - 1): it + 2]:
            for a in GRID_A[max(0, ia - 1): ia + 2]:
                prm = dict(p_copy=pc, tau=tau, a=a, q_core=qc)
                L = evaluate(prm)[0]
                if L < best[0]:
                    best = (L, prm)
    emit_fn(f"    stage C ({len(cache)} evals): best loss {best[0]:.2f}")
    L, parts, g = evaluate(best[1])
    return dict(params=best[1], loss=L, parts=parts, gen=g, real=real, n_evals=len(cache), wrap=prod.wrap.sizes)


# ======================================================================= one transliteration
def run_translit(T, by, emit_fn, t_start, out_dir: Path, real_name="real"):
    train_names, held_names = G1.split_names(by)
    train = [(p, by[p]) for p in train_names]
    test = [(p, by[p]) for p in held_names]
    tr_tok = [w for _, ls in train for l in ls for w in l]
    seg = SlotSegmenter(tr_tok)
    emit_fn(f"=== {T}: {len(by)} pages; training {len(train)} pages ({len(tr_tok)} tokens), held-out {len(test)} pages "
            f"({sum(len(l) for _, ls in test for l in ls)} tokens); training SlotSegmenter {len(seg.prefixes)} prefix / {len(seg.suffixes)} suffix candidates ===")
    t0 = time.time()
    F = fit([ls for _, ls in train], seg, emit_fn, t0)
    prm = F["params"]
    emit_fn(f"  wrapper tables (counted): {F['wrap']['ctx2']} (pos, pre-1, suf-1) contexts, {F['wrap']['ctx1']} (pos, suf-1), "
            f"{F['wrap']['ctx0']} (pos); {F['wrap']['outcomes']} distinct (pre, suf) outcomes")
    emit_fn(f"  fit ({F['n_evals']} grid evaluations, {time.time() - t0:.0f}s): p_copy {prm['p_copy']}, tau {prm['tau']}, a {prm['a']}, "
            f"q_core {prm['q_core']}; loss {F['loss']:.2f} (R {F['parts'][0]:.2f}, shares {F['parts'][1]:.2f}, types {F['parts'][2]:.2f})")
    r, g = F["real"], F["gen"]
    emit_fn("  [in-sample] target R(d) real : " + " ".join(f"{x:.3f}" for x in r["R"]))
    emit_fn("  [in-sample] fitted R(d) TL s0: " + " ".join(f"{x:.3f}" for x in g["R"]))
    emit_fn("  [in-sample] edit shares real : " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v:.4f}" for k, v in zip(EDIT_KINDS, r["shares"])) + f"  (counts {r['counts'].astype(int).tolist()})")
    emit_fn("  [in-sample] edit shares TL s0: " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v:.4f}" for k, v in zip(EDIT_KINDS, g["shares"])) + f"  (counts {g['counts'].astype(int).tolist()})")
    emit_fn(f"  [in-sample] types real {r['types']} at {r['tokens']} tokens; TL seed 0 {g['types']} at {g['tokens']} tokens")
    lr, lg = np.array(r["lens"]), np.array(g["lens"])
    emit_fn(f"  [in-sample] line length real mean {lr.mean():.3f} sd {lr.std():.3f}; TL seed 0 mean {lg.mean():.3f} sd {lg.std():.3f} (empirical sampling)")
    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (out_dir / f"fit_{T}.json").write_text(json.dumps(dict(
        translit=T, params=prm, W=W, free_parameters=4, loss=F["loss"], loss_parts=F["parts"], n_evals=F["n_evals"],
        wrapper_tables=F["wrap"],
        target=dict(R=r["R"].tolist(), shares=r["shares"].tolist(), types=r["types"], tokens=r["tokens"]),
        fitted=dict(R=g["R"].tolist(), shares=g["shares"].tolist(), types=g["types"], tokens=g["tokens"]),
        method="staged grid (A p_copy x tau x a at q_core=.25; B q_core 0..1 step .1; C local p/tau/a), seed 0, common random numbers",
    ), indent=1), encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")
    # ---- generate
    prod = TLProducer([ls for _, ls in train], seg)
    tr_counts = [len(ls) for _, ls in train]
    gens = {}
    for kind, pp in (("TL", prm), ("TL0", dict(prm, p_copy=0.0))):
        prod.set_params(pp)
        gens[kind] = []
        for s in (1, 2, 3):
            te_counts = random.Random(s).sample(tr_counts, len(test))
            pages = prod.text(s, tr_counts + te_counts)
            gtr = [(f"g{i}", pages[i]) for i in range(len(train))]
            gte = [(f"h{i}", pages[len(train) + i]) for i in range(len(test))]
            gens[kind].append((gtr, gte))
            side = dict(source=f"s58 {kind} two-layer producer fitted on {T} training pages, seed {s}", params=pp,
                        pages=[dict(id=p, section="S58", hand="S58", lang="?", quire="?", lines=ls,
                                    role="train" if i < len(train) else "heldout") for i, (p, ls) in enumerate(gtr + gte)])
            (out_dir / f"{kind}_{T}_s{s}.meta.json").write_text(json.dumps(side), encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")
    t1 = time.time()
    real_m = S57.Measured(f"{T} {real_name}", train, test)
    ms = {k: [S57.Measured(f"{T} {k} s{i + 1}", a, b) for i, (a, b) in enumerate(gens[k])] for k in LABELS}
    emit_fn(f"  measured 7 texts in {time.time() - t1:.0f}s")
    if time.time() - t_start > STEP_LIMIT * 2:
        raise TimeoutError("run exceeded 60 minutes")
    off = {"ZL3b": 0, "RF1b": 10, "IT2a": 20}.get(T, 30)
    t2 = time.time()
    real_dr = S57.draws_for([real_m], S57.SEED + off)
    drs = {"TL": S57.draws_for(ms["TL"], S57.SEED + off + 1), "TL0": S57.draws_for(ms["TL0"], S57.SEED + off + 2)}
    emit_fn(f"  subsample draws {time.time() - t2:.0f}s")
    real_pt = real_m.point()
    pts = {k: S57.mean_point(ms[k]) for k in LABELS}
    real_ci = {k: S57.pct(real_dr[k]) for k in S57.DRAW_KEYS}
    emit_fn(f"  real held-out: Moran {real_pt['P1']:.4f} [{real_ci['P1'][0]:.4f},{real_ci['P1'][1]:.4f}]; core->core {real_pt['P2']:+.4f} "
            f"[{real_ci['P2'][0]:+.4f},{real_ci['P2'][1]:+.4f}]; prefix gain {real_pt['P3']:+.4f} [{real_ci['P3'][0]:+.4f},{real_ci['P3'][1]:+.4f}]; "
            f"jsd_first_fg {real_pt['P4']:.4f} (excess {real_pt['P4_exc']:+.4f}); CHARWIN {real_pt['P5']:+.4f}")
    emit_fn("  real F1 by stream: " + ", ".join(f"{k[3:]} {real_pt[k]:+.4f} [{real_ci[k][0]:+.4f},{real_ci[k][1]:+.4f}]" for k in ("F1_prefix", "F1_core", "F1_suffix"))
            + f" -> s39 rule on the real text (this split): {S57.f1_layer_call(real_ci)}")
    for lab in LABELS:
        for i, p in enumerate(pts[lab][1]):
            emit_fn(f"    {lab} s{i + 1}: Moran {p['P1']:.4f} core->core {p['P2']:+.4f} prefix gain {p['P3']:+.4f} jsd_first_fg {p['P4']:.4f} "
                    f"CHARWIN {p['P5']:+.4f} F1 prefix/core/suffix {p['F1_prefix']:+.4f}/{p['F1_core']:+.4f}/{p['F1_suffix']:+.4f}")
    res = {}
    for lab in LABELS:
        cells = S57.score_cells(real_pt, real_dr, pts[lab][0], drs[lab])
        n = sum(1 for v in cells.values() if v[0])
        emit_fn(f"  -- {lab}: {n}/6 hold --")
        for k, (ok, txt) in cells.items():
            emit_fn(f"    {k} {'HOLDS' if ok else 'fails'}: {txt}")
        res[lab] = dict(n=n, holds={k: bool(v[0]) for k, v in cells.items()}, text={k: v[1] for k, v in cells.items()})
    res["fit"] = dict(params=prm, loss=F["loss"], parts=F["parts"])
    res["real_point"] = real_pt; res["real_ci"] = real_ci
    res["TL_point"] = pts["TL"][0]; res["TL0_point"] = pts["TL0"][0]
    return res


# ======================================================================= fixture (synthetic, no real data)
def fixture():
    out_lines = []

    def say(s=""):
        print(s, flush=True)
        out_lines.append(s)

    t0 = time.time()
    say(f"s58 fixture; stub_match: {stub_match()}")
    rng = random.Random(5)
    alph = "abcdefghij"
    pres = ["", "", "q", "o", "ch", "sh", "d"]
    sufs = ["", "", "y", "dy", "in", "ol", "r"]
    cores = sorted({"".join(rng.choice(alph) for _ in range(rng.randint(1, 4))) for _ in range(600)})
    cw = [1 + 200 / (1 + i) for i in range(len(cores))]
    # pseudo training text with an ordered affix layer: prefix of t follows suffix of t-1 (70 %), line-final suffix bias
    base = []
    for _ in range(60):
        lines = []
        for _ in range(14):
            L = rng.randint(5, 10)
            line, ps = [], None
            for i in range(L):
                p = pres[(sufs.index(ps) + 1) % len(pres)] if ps is not None and rng.random() < 0.7 else rng.choice(pres)
                s = "r" if i == L - 1 and rng.random() < 0.5 else rng.choice(sufs)
                line.append(p + rng.choices(cores, cw)[0] + s); ps = s
            lines.append(line)
        base.append(lines)
    seg0 = SlotSegmenter([w for ls in base for l in ls for w in l])
    truth = dict(p_copy=0.2, tau=4.0, a=0.15, q_core=0.2)
    pr = TLProducer(base, seg0)
    pr.set_params(truth)
    pages = pr.text(99, [14] * 120)
    by = OrderedDict((f"f{i}", ls) for i, ls in enumerate(pages))
    say(f"fixture: synthetic text {len(by)} pages, {sum(len(l) for ls in pages for l in ls)} tokens, truth {truth}")
    nd = S57.N_DRAW
    S57.N_DRAW = 40
    try:
        res = run_translit("FIX", by, say, t0, RUNS / "fixture", real_name="synthetic")
    finally:
        S57.N_DRAW = nd
    fp = res["fit"]["params"]
    ok1 = abs(fp["p_copy"] - truth["p_copy"]) <= 0.08
    ok2 = res["TL"]["holds"]["P3"]
    say(f"  fixture check: fitted p_copy {fp['p_copy']} vs truth {truth['p_copy']} -> {'OK' if ok1 else 'FAIL'}; "
        f"refit TL holds P3 (ordered wrapper recovered) on its own held-out pages -> {'OK' if ok2 else 'FAIL'}")
    say(f"  fixture TL {res['TL']['n']}/6, TL0 {res['TL0']['n']}/6 (informative only)")
    ok = ok1 and ok2
    say(f"FIXTURE {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} ({time.time() - t0:.0f}s)")
    RUNS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (RUNS / "fixture.txt").write_text("\n".join(out_lines) + "\n", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")
    return ok


# ======================================================================= main
def main():
    t0 = time.time()
    emit("s58 -- two-layer producer TL (counted ordered affix wrapper over s57's local-memory core stream) fitted on the "
         "training pages, predicting s57's 6 properties of the 41 held-out pages")
    emit(f"date: {S57.clock()}")
    emit(f"sha256 s58_two_layer_heldout.py: {sha256(SELF)}")
    emit(f"sha256 s58_two_layer_heldout.prereg.sha256: {sha256(STUB) if STUB.exists() else 'missing'}")
    emit(f"stub_match: {stub_match()}")
    for m in S57.local_modules():
        emit(f"  local import {m} sha256={sha256(ROOT / m)}")
    emit(f"numpy {np.__version__}; python -I; CPU; W={W}; grid p_copy {GRID_P}, tau {GRID_TAU}, a {GRID_A}, q_core {GRID_QC}; "
         f"subsample {int(S57.SUB_FRAC * 100)} % of held-out pages without replacement x {S57.N_DRAW}; core->core null "
         f"{S57.N_SHUF_POINT} (point) / {S57.N_SHUF_DRAW} (per draw); seeds 1-3; scoring = s57 code imported")
    emit("")
    allres = {}
    for T, f in TRANSLITS.items():
        path = ROOT / "data" / "translit" / f"{f}.meta.json"
        emit(f"translit {T}: {path.name} sha256={sha256(path)[:16]}")
        by = S57.load_meta(path)
        allres[T] = run_translit(T, by, emit, t0, RUNS)
        emit(f"  elapsed so far {time.time() - t0:.0f}s")
        emit("")
        OUT.write_text("\n".join(log) + "\n", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")

    emit("=== VERDICT (pre-registered rule) ===")
    for lab in LABELS:
        row = []
        for T in TRANSLITS:
            h = allres[T][lab]["holds"]
            row.append(f"{T} {allres[T][lab]['n']}/6 [" + " ".join(f"{k}{'+' if v else '-'}" for k, v in h.items()) + "]")
        emit(f"  {lab:4}: " + "; ".join(row))
    emit("  s57 as filed (not rerun): local-memory ZL3b 0/6, RF1b 0/6, IT2a 0/6; null p_copy=0 1/6 each")
    z = allres["ZL3b"]["TL"]
    sets = {T: tuple(sorted(k for k, v in allres[T]["TL"]["holds"].items() if v)) for T in TRANSLITS}
    if z["n"] >= 5 and sets["RF1b"] == sets["ZL3b"] and sets["IT2a"] == sets["ZL3b"]:
        verdict = "two-layer model predicts untouched pages"
    elif z["n"] >= 5:
        verdict = "holds on ZL3b only, not stable across transliterations"
    else:
        verdict = "two-layer model does NOT predict untouched pages"
    emit(f"VERDICT: {verdict} (ZL3b {z['n']}/6; holding sets {sets})")
    emit(f"TL0 (p_copy=0) counts: " + ", ".join(f"{T} {allres[T]['TL0']['n']}/6" for T in TRANSLITS))
    for T in TRANSLITS:
        a, b = allres[T]["TL"]["holds"], allres[T]["TL0"]["holds"]
        only_tl = [k for k in a if a[k] and not b[k]]
        only_tl0 = [k for k in a if b[k] and not a[k]]
        emit(f"  {T}: held by TL not TL0: {only_tl or 'none'}; held by TL0 not TL: {only_tl0 or 'none'}")
    emit("caveats: P6 weak (the s39 rule gives a different call on each transliteration's real text for this split); "
         "P4 and P3 close to built-in via the counted wrapper; TL vs TL0 isolates the core-memory contribution")
    RUNS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (RUNS / "cells.json").write_text(json.dumps(allres, indent=1, default=lambda o: o.tolist() if hasattr(o, "tolist") else str(o)),
                                     encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")
    emit("")
    emit(f"elapsed: {time.time() - t0:.1f} s")
    emit(f"date end: {S57.clock()}")
    emit(f"paths: {OUT}, {RUNS}")
    OUT.write_text("\n".join(log) + "\n", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    if "--fixture" in sys.argv:
        sys.exit(0 if fixture() else 1)
    main()
